{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe duration investigation reconstructed end-to-end `review-plan` and gated-close wall time from Codex rollout logs and tracker sidecars using a temporary read-only probe. The operator asked that this probe live under the project `scripts/` directory for reuse. The temporary version contains machine-specific paths and snapshot bounds, so the repository version must expose those as CLI inputs rather than bake them into source.\n\n## CLI contract and frozen example\nRepository-neutral defaults are explicit:\n- Repeatable `--log-root PATH` defaults to `~/.codex/sessions` and `~/.codex/archived_sessions`, resolved with `Path.home()`; no literal user-home path is stored.\n- `--tracker PATH` defaults to `.tickets-tracker` relative to the invocation working directory.\n- `--since` and `--until` are optional ISO-8601 bounds; omission means unbounded on that side.\n- `--provider-prefix` is optional; omission accepts any actual provider while still requiring positive `metrics.llm_calls`.\n- `--current-since` is optional; omission suppresses the current-regime sensitivity. The single term `current regime` is used throughout.\n\nThe frozen analysis is reproduced with: `python scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py summary --tracker .tickets-tracker --since 2026-08-07T12:34:40Z --until 2026-08-23T21:15:00Z --provider-prefix bedrock: --current-since 2026-08-22T00:00:00Z`. The current-regime cutoff is therefore exactly `2026-08-22T00:00:00Z`; it is an explicit analysis argument, not a source-code default.\n\n## Plan\n- Add `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py` as a read-only, standard-library-only CLI. It links top-level Codex shell invocations through yielded cells and PTY polls, resolves ticket aliases, matches model-backed gate sidecars, and reports end-to-end percentiles. It performs no filesystem scan or other work at import time so the clean-wheel standalone import walk remains valid.\n- Preserve the existing modes (`summary`, `table`, `clean`, `all`, and `unmatched`) while applying the CLI contract above.\n- Add a gated-close phase breakdown. Read `COMPLETION_VERDICT`, closing `STATUS`, and completion `SIGNATURE` timestamps directly. Report sidecar `det_ms` and `llm_ms` directly. Infer pre-verifier residual as `verdict_timestamp - total_ms - command_start`, and report remaining verifier/post-write residuals separately.\n- Label every phase as direct metric, direct event interval, or inferred residual; do not imply an uninstrumented boundary is directly observed.\n- Add focused synthetic tests for command classification, terminal reconstruction, percentile calculation, cohort filtering, and close-phase decomposition. Tests must not read the live tracker or user session logs.\n- Run `python scripts/check_import_walk.py` in addition to focused pytest and Ruff checks. If a non-stdlib optional dependency becomes necessary, declare it in `scripts/check_import_walk.py` `EXPECTED_OPTIONAL`; the planned implementation does not need one.\n- Do not change agent-duration guidance in this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The reusable probe is stored at `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py`.\n- [ ] Source contains no literal machine-specific user-home or worktree path.\n- [ ] The documented command reproduces the frozen provider-clean window.\n- [ ] `--current-since 2026-08-22T00:00:00Z` selects the frozen current-regime cohort.\n- [ ] No-LLM operations remain distinguishable from completed model-backed cohorts.\n- [ ] Forced, status/check/help, unmatched, and interrupted operations remain distinguishable from completed model-backed cohorts.\n- [ ] Gated-close output reports pre-verifier residual, deterministic verifier, LLM verifier, verdict-to-status, status-to-signature, and remaining post-write tail when the required evidence exists.\n- [ ] Each gated-close phase is labeled as a direct metric, direct event interval, or inferred residual.\n- [ ] Focused tests use synthetic fixtures only and pass.\n- [ ] The standalone script passes the import-walk check without import-time side effects.\n- [ ] Repository guidance remains unchanged pending separate operator confirmation."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787527719097099001,"uuid":"dd590a18-5174-4c35-9370-cc929e1d6656"}